    {
      "id": "claim_22761e564f074295b6d235fc0410b695",
      "statement": "The QuickJS REPL provides capability-based isolation rather than OS isolation: the context has no ambient filesystem, network, fetch, require, process, or real-clock capability, with authority added only through programmatic tool calling; it defaults to a 64 MiB runtime memory limit and 256 per-eval PTC host-call budget, while its 5-second timeout bounds QuickJS VM execution but not time awaiting Python host calls.",
      "evidence": [
